
Written:
  /srv/mnema/.env   (secrets inside, mode 600)
  /srv/mnema/docker-compose.yml

Owner account for the first sign-in:
  user      owner
  password  example-password
  (also in .env as ADMIN_INITIAL_PASSWORD)

What to do next:
  1. Start it, in the folder with the two files:
       docker compose up -d --wait
  2. Put HTTPS in front: set up a reverse proxy (Caddy, nginx, Nginx Proxy Manager, DSM) that forwards https://chat.example.com to http://127.0.0.1:8080 with WebSocket support. It carries the web page and chat only, not voice.
  3. Open https://chat.example.com in your browser.
  4. Sign in as "owner" with the password above.
  5. Change the password (your profile settings, Password), then delete the ADMIN_INITIAL_PASSWORD line from .env.
  6. Forward these three ports from your router to this machine (never 8080) and allow them in its firewall:
       443/tcp                the web page, to the reverse proxy
       50000-50050/udp        voice and video
       3479/udp and 3479/tcp  relay for members behind strict firewalls
  7. Check it from outside: open Admin > Status and press "Test my connection", best from a phone on mobile data instead of your Wi-Fi. The same test also reads how many members your internet upload can serve a screen share to (it cannot be measured from inside your network, so no number is shown here). From a shell: docker compose exec app mnema-talk doctor

Update later: docker compose pull && docker compose up -d
